In the said rulings of respondent No.3, their lordship have laid down the following principles;
SCCH 5 'If any owner of the vehicle with gross negligent manner allowed a person to drive vehicle,
whoever not holding valid driving licence, then Insurance Company will not be fastened with liability of pay and recover, which is clear breach of policy conditions and compensation should be only liable to pay by the owner himself etc.,'
